---
/**
 * /en/about/ — tłumaczenie /o-projekcie/ (src/pages/o-projekcie/index.astro): ten sam układ, teksty z src/data/en/o-serwisie.ts.
 * Kalendarz zmian (ActivityCalendar, commitHistory) opisuje polskie commity — tu go nie ma; jedno zdanie odsyła do strony polskiej.
 * Kotwice: #why, #principles, #how-we-work, #who-runs-the-site, #funding, #change-history, #corrections. Para i stempel w src/i18n/pages.json.
 * Rejestr sprostowań: wpisy `correction: true` z historii zmian tłumaczeń (te same co w oryginałach).
 */
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '@/components/layout/Section.astro';
import PageHeader from '@/components/layout/PageHeader.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/layout/PageMeta.astro';
import Prose from '@/components/article/Prose.astro';
import NumberedList from '@/components/blocks/NumberedList.astro';
import PageTranslationNote from '@/components/article/PageTranslationNote.astro';
import Changelog from '@/components/article/Changelog.astro';
import { contact, editorialRules, legalPages } from '@/data/en/o-serwisie';
import { pagePairOf } from '@/i18n/pages';
import { enHref, getTranslations } from '@/i18n/translations';
import type { Crumb, SeoInput } from '@/lib/seo';

const page = legalPages.oProjekcie;
const crumbs: Crumb[] = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/en/' }, { label: page.title }];
const seo: SeoInput = {
  title: page.docTitle,
  description: page.description,
  index: !pagePairOf(Astro.url.pathname)?.draft,
  breadcrumbs: crumbs,
  page: { type: 'AboutPage' },
};
// Corrections register: correction entries from the change history of published translations, newest first
const corrections = (await getTranslations())
  .filter((t) => !t.article.data.noindex)
  .flatMap((t) => (t.article.data.changelog ?? []).filter((e) => e.correction).map((e) => ({ date: e.date, text: `[${t.article.data.title}](${enHref(t)}#change-history): ${e.text}` })))
  .sort((a, b) => b.date.getTime() - a.date.getTime());
const mail = `mailto:${contact.email}`;
---
<BaseLayout seo={seo}>
  <Section space="bottom" class="about-top">
    <PageHeader title={page.title} lead={page.lead} eyebrow="About the site" crumbs={crumbs}>
      <PageMeta items={[{ label: 'Updated', value: page.updated }, { label: 'Contact', value: contact.email }]} />
    </PageHeader>
  </Section>

  <Section space="bottom">
    <PageTranslationNote />
    <Prose>
      <p>In Poland, pay from public money in healthcare is only partly transparent. We know the statutory minimum wages and individual contracts, but nobody adds up how much in total goes to one person from several workplaces.</p>

      <h2 id="why">Why this site exists</h2>
      <p>We gather what can be established from publicly available sources — data, audit reports, court judgments, replies to requests for access to public information — and we show what cannot be established. We describe how the system works: where the money comes from, how it reaches hospitals and doctors, why there are staff shortages and what the statistics do not show.</p>
      <p>We are not against doctors. We are in favour of public money being visible. That is why we call for <a href="/en/demand/">public total payments for each person, under a permanent identifier and without names</a> (in Polish).</p>

      <h2 id="principles">Editorial principles</h2>
      <NumberedList items={editorialRules} />

      <h2 id="how-we-work">How the texts are made</h2>
      <p>We prepare the texts with the help of AI tools: for finding and organising sources, calculations, first drafts, translations into English and the site’s code. A human is in charge of the content: the editors choose the topics, decide on the arguments and approve every publication and every correction after reading the changes.</p>
      <p>A tool is not a source. Every number and every claim has a footnote to a document, data set or legal act, and the editors are responsible for errors — report them, and we will record the correction in the change history below the text.</p>
      <h2 id="who-runs-the-site">Who runs the site</h2>
      <p>The site is run anonymously. No foundation, company or organisation stands behind it. Judge us by our sources: every number has a footnote with a link to a document you can check yourself.</p>
      <h2 id="funding">Funding</h2>
      <p>The site is non-commercial: it has no advertising, paid content or sponsors. The only outside money is voluntary donations from readers through <a href="https://suppi.pl/zarobkilekarzy" hreflang="pl">Suppi</a> (in Polish) — with nothing in return and no influence on the choice of topics or the content.</p>

      <h2 id="change-history">Change history</h2>
      <p>The site’s code and content are public, and every change stays in the repository history with a date; a calendar of these changes is on the <a href="/o-projekcie/#historia-zmian" hreflang="pl">Polish version of this page</a> (in Polish).</p>

      <h2 id="corrections">Corrections and contact</h2>
      <p>Spotted an error, an out-of-date number or a source that no longer works? Write to <a href={mail}>{contact.email}</a>. We check every report.</p>
      <p>Every substantive change — new data, a change in the matter described, the correction of an error — has a dated entry in the change history below the text, and a text’s update date is the date of the latest such entry. We do not record typos or changes in appearance. We also list corrections of errors here:</p>
      {corrections.length > 0
        ? <Changelog title="Corrections register" id="corrections-register" entries={corrections} />
        : <p>We have not published any corrections so far.</p>}
      <p>The site is for information only and does not give medical or legal advice. How we handle data is described in the <a href="/prywatnosc/" hreflang="pl">privacy policy</a> (in Polish), and we answer the most common objections in <a href="/en/faq/">a separate text</a>.</p>
    </Prose>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-top { padding-top: clamp(32px, 4vw, 56px); }
</style>
